# StudyFlow Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack

- Use Next.js App Router with TypeScript.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Do not use the `any` type unless absolutely necessary.

## Forms

- Use React Hook Form for all forms.
- Use Zod for validation.
- Every form must include visible labels and validation error messages.
- Disable submit buttons while forms are submitting.

## Data

- Store user settings in localStorage until a backend is added.
- Validate any data loaded from localStorage before using it.
- Handle invalid or missing data gracefully.

## Components

- Create reusable components instead of duplicating UI.
- Keep business logic separate from UI where possible.

## Accessibility

- Every form input must have an associated label.
- Ensure keyboard navigation works correctly.
- Display validation errors using accessible markup.

## AI Output

- Verify all AI-generated code by running the application.
- Run tests before considering a feature complete.
- Never assume AI-generated code is correct without verification.
